# Auth & Authorization

## Guards and decorators

| Piece | Path | Use |
|-------|------|-----|
| `JwtGuard` | `auth/guards/jwt.guard.ts` | Require valid JWT |
| `RolesGuard` | `auth/guards/roles-guard.ts` | Enforce `@Roles()` metadata |
| `@Roles(...)` | `auth/decorators/roles.decorator.ts` | Allowed `UserRoleEnum` values |
| `@LoggedInUser()` | `shared/decorators/logged-in-user.decorator.ts` | Inject authenticated `User` |

## Endpoint patterns

**Admin CRUD** — class or method level:

```ts
@UseGuards(JwtGuard, RolesGuard)
@Roles(UserRoleEnum.Admin)
```

**Self-service (`/me`)** — authenticated user only, no role check:

```ts
@Controller('me')
@UseGuards(JwtGuard)
export class MeController {
  @Get()
  get(@LoggedInUser() user: User) { ... }
}
```

## Rules

- Admin list/create/update/delete on entity controllers (`users`, `tasks`, …) — `JwtGuard` + `RolesGuard` + `@Roles`.
- Current-user profile and settings — `MeController` or `me`-scoped routes; use `@LoggedInUser()`, not URL `:id` from client input alone.
- Role values from `UserRoleEnum` in `@app/contracts` only.
- Public routes (login, contact form) — no JWT guard; still validate body with contract commands.

## Reference

- Admin: `backend/src/users/controllers/users.controller.ts`
- Self: `backend/src/me/controllers/me.controller.ts`
